The long-awaited moment has arrived - patch 1.05 is now available!

We have published a patch that introduces a number of changes to the game. Without further ado, here are the patch notes: 

 stabilization of the main storyline (compasses, logs, pointers corrected);
 fixed reported issues (bugs and errors);
 contracts and new side quests added;
 crafting system added;
 trade stabilization, new NPCs and improvements to existing ones;
 pack of new 10 bosses; 
 added fast travel system and teleporters
 ADDED MINIMAP [M button].


Some of the new features have been added according to your suggestions and comments. We are constantly following your bugs and suggestions for changes and we will modify M.E.A.T. accordingly so that we can provide you with as much positive experience as possible.

But this is not the end

We still ask for your support in reporting any bugs or suggestions on a regular basis. Thanks to them we know what to focus on and in which direction to direct our work. We are grateful for every opinion (both favorable and less favorable) because thanks to them we are heading in the right direction.

In the meantime, let us know what you think about today's patch and what you'd like to see in the next one (I'll tell you right away - we're working on SFX all the time). We'll review your responses and work to implement your suggested changes/improvements on an ongoing basis.

Fixing a number of bugs found in the game

As reported, we have fixed a large number of bugs that were present in a percentage of players.  These include:

 updated the music manager - smoother transitions, new soundtracks, split between underground and above ground music;
 partially fixed a bug with freezing mobs (if you change the game language during gameplay and do not restart it, you cannot use the skill bar - bug will be fixed in the next patch)
 increased visibility on the minimap;
 added a TIPS panel to the PLAYER PANEL; 
 zero ammo bug fixed;
 added new monsters to existing locations;
 side quests have been updated and the player compass has been improved;
 improved quest log entries and gameplay for problematic main quests (including the Red Button quest);
 new special skill icon graphics have been added.

Thank you for your support

We are very grateful for the information you provide us through Steam and other social media. They help us in the ongoing improvement of the game. We assure you that we are looking into every bug and putting it in the submission queue. 

In the meantime, we are also adding new content to the game, thanks to which the time you spend in Washagami will increase significantly. 
Do you own M.E.A.T.? Leave a review!

If you are a lucky owner of our game, we ask you to leave a proper review on our store! This way we will be able to collect more feedback from you and increase our visibility on Steam.

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/38078745/7b99a372d5aa1047f93f51074fb71fbb373466ec.png

Hotfixes to M.E.A.T.

We want you to know that after the release of M.E.A.T. we are not idle and are already working on changes to the game. All you have to do is restart Steam and download the update, which is now available. Below you will find the changes we have added to M.E.A.T.: 


 balancing the gameplay;
 there was a problem with the compass in some quests - this has been resolved;
 kill counter works properly now;
 bug in quick travel system has been fixed.

Report any bugs to us through the Community Center

If you encounter any bugs, please let us know in the subforum named "Bugs". We will continuously analyze the bugs and eliminate them in hotfixes.

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/38078745/df2f9737c85d04ee229747399e6ce91b9327a2d0.png

In the New Year discover the mystery of the Washagami!

Dear M.E.A.T. Lovers,

2021 greets us with new mechanics and quests  in the M.E.A.T. OPEN BETA . In the sweat of the last hour we worked on this build to introduce you to the following news:

 the ability to autoload items;
 improved game performance;
 added two more quests (currently you can complete 5 quests);
 added a new location (crypt);
 ESC button allows to minimize the interface of the loot, toolbar and crates;
 improved the display of information at the tables;
 highlighting of objects (boxes, monsters, NPC) after hovering the cursor over them;
 fixed bug with fading layers;
 dialog system has been improved;
 introducing NPC dialogue randomization system.


What about the bugs you have reported so far?

As you can see, there is a lot of news.  As usual, we are counting on your support. Share your opinion and  report any bugs to us via our Steam forum. 

If in this version we didn't fix a bug that you recently reported to us - don't worry! We are constantly analyzing and modifying the in-game content and each of the issues you submit is in our report file. 

Thank you for all your help!

Last year was full of challenges for us. Taking on the first big project, which was the M.E.A.T., creating a great community of players involved in the creative process of the game and organizing a team that could turn the dream of creating games into reality.

This is all thanks to your support, for which we are grateful!

We wish you a happy New Year, many great titles from other creators, an unstoppable love for games and equipment that allows you to run every game on ultra! 

The whole Trippin Bears team wishes you best!

New mechanics in OPEN BETA!
Dear M.E.A.T. Lovers,

Tomorrow, i.e. 09.12.2020 at 23:00 GMT +1 we will publish a new version of the game's OPEN BETA. You will find in our update, among other things:

 trading system with NPCs encountered during your trip;
 first quests connected to the M.E.A.T. storyline;
 most of the bugs you have reported have been fixed;
 improved mob selecting mechanics;
 new selecting mob mechanic with the use of keyboard button (at the moment it is "E" button).

We hope that you will once again enter the world of M.E.A.T. and immerse yourself in a picturesque world of Washagami. As always, we ask you to report any bugs or suggestions on our Steam forum.

How to become a tester?

If you want to join the group of testers, send an email to kontakt@meatrpg.com, adding "GAME TESTING" in the title of the message and you will receive a special Steam access code.

But remember one thing...

...after the end of the open BETA tests, the key you received will be automatically deactivated and access to the game will only be possible if you purchase a full version.
